The authors recast the Mukhanov–Sasaki equation for curvature and tensor perturbations as a time-independent Schrödinger equation on the half-line $(-\infty, 0)$ with effective potentials $V_s(\eta) = z''/z$ and $V_t(\eta) = a''/a$. They identify the Bunch–Davies initial condition with the Jost solution asymptotic to $e^{-ik\eta}$ as $\eta 	o -\infty$, and express the freeze-out amplitude of the growing mode via the Jost function $F_{
u - 1/2}(k)$. The primordial power spectra are then written as $\mathcal{P}(k) \propto 1/|F(k)|^2$. Using inverse-scattering theory, specifically the Marchenko equation linearized via the Born approximation in the large-$k$ limit, they reconstruct $V_s$ and $V_t$ from synthetic spectra generated by known benchmark potentials (quadratic and step-like).



